</section>

<section class="cp-topic" id="economy-reference">
<h2>Reading the slides</h2>
<p>The source and year behind each economy figure, and what the comparison areas on the Wages slides cover, are listed on each slide. Note that some side-by-side figures do not have matching data years, for example the Marine Economy Total Jobs slide. In instances where data years are different, figures are kept separate.</p>

<h3 id="economy-symbols">Symbols on the slides</h3>
<p>Each symbol sits on a label, not on a number, and is explained in a key on the slide and in words for screen readers. All survive a greyscale print.</p>
<dl class="cp-reasons">
<div><dt>&#8224;</dt><dd>The headline year (marine economy: 2025 for businesses, jobs and wages).</dd></div>
<div><dt>&#8225;</dt><dd>The year before (marine economy GDP, 2024).</dd></div>
<div><dt>*</dt><dd>A total that leaves something out: withheld sectors, or Public administration GDP.</dd></div>
<div><dt>&#167;</dt><dd>A sector withheld entirely. Not used for Public administration, whose jobs and wages are shown; the asterisk on GDP covers it.</dd></div>
<div><dt>&#8776;</dt><dd>An <a href="#estimated">estimate</a>. Also a diagonal hatch on bars and a dashed ring on dots.</dd></div>
</dl>

<h3 id="sectors-not-shown">Sectors missing from a county's Wages chart</h3>
<p>The Wages chart shows average wage per job, so a sector with no jobs in a county has nothing to average and is left off. That is a zero, not a withheld value: several counties have no ship and boat building, for example. The county's other charts, such as Business Diversity, still show the zero.</p>

<h3 id="marine-jobs">Why there is no "marine jobs at risk" figure</h3>
<p>NOAA's original snapshot counted marine businesses in the floodplain, using licensed business location data that cannot be reused. The open alternative, Census LEHD job counts by location, only identifies broad (2-digit) industries, while the marine sectors are defined at up to 6 digits. No open source places marine jobs on a map, so the figure is left out.</p>
</section>
